 R←Test_34(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;ALIEN;list;fno;crash;own;QEN
⍝ `API.Process`, called with the name of a parameter space (as `SetTrap` does), saves the variables
⍝ visible where the error occurred, and the stack holds none of HandleError's own functions (API included)
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

⍝ Preconditions...
 #.⎕SHADOW'HandleErrorParms'
 #.HandleErrorParms←##.HandleError.API.CreateParms
 #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder←GetTempPath⊃⎕SI
 #.HandleErrorParms.saveErrorWS←0
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 {}'CREATE!'FilesAndDirs.CheckPath #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 ALIEN←'Hello world'

 ⎕TRAP←(405 'E' '406 ##.HandleError.API.Process ''#.HandleErrorParms''')(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 :Trap 406
     {⎕SIGNAL ⍵}405
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1
 :EndTrap

 QEN←⎕EN
 →T.GoToTidyUp 406≠QEN
 list←FilesAndDirs.ListFiles #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder,'/*.dcf'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢list
 fno←(⊃list)⎕FTIE 0
 crash←⎕FREAD fno 1
 ⎕FUNTIE fno
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠crash.⎕NC'Vars'
 →T.GoToTidyUp'Hello world'≢crash.Vars.ALIEN
 own←(⍕##.HandleError),'.'
 →T.GoToTidyUp∨/(⊂own)≡¨(≢own)↑¨crash.XSI

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
